    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22671" root="شفه" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْفَهُ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُفَاهِىٌّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Accord. to some,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْفَى</span>
signifies A man <i>whose lips do not close together:</i>
(S, K:) but there is no proof of its correctness:
(S:) the fem. in this sense is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَفْيَآءُ</span>. (TA in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شفى</span>.)

